  "experiment_id": "sec-cross-strategy-residual-allocator-v3",
  "description": "Rerun of the v2 sealed allocator against a corrected instrument classification map. v2's concentration inputs misclassified nine exchange traded products as issuers, most importantly SLV, which reached 21.5% and 26.8% de-levered weight in the two sources and was therefore reported as the largest single issuer. Returns, stresses, breadth and bootstrap are unchanged by the fix; only concentration is affected.",
  "supersedes": "sec-cross-strategy-residual-allocator-v2",
  "v1_defects_addressed": [
    "v1 never inspected holdings, so it could not detect that the two strategies hold largely the same names.",
    "v1 charged outer reallocation cost only on the allocator weight change; the selected static rule therefore had zero turnover inside the locked window and the doubled-cost stress was a no-op.",
    "v1 delayed only a constant weight series, so both delay stresses were no-ops inside the locked window.",
    "v1 applied the sleeve shock at the midpoint of the full frame, which lies inside the development period and never touched the locked window.",
    "v1 ran no missing-stock stress and no exact-daily reconciliation.",
    "v2 used concentration map v1, whose hand-written exchange-traded list omitted SLV, XLB, XLP, XLV, XLY, VTV, VWO, BIL and PDBC. Unlisted funds fell through to the issuer bucket, overstating single-issuer concentration and understating fund concentration."
  ],
